{
 "id": "lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual",
 "blueprint": {
  "is": "lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual",
  "from": null,
  "same_as": []
 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Punctual upper bound in a relative affine curve",
 "statement": "Let $Y_0$ be a separated $k_0$-scheme of finite type and let\n$h:U_0\\to Y_0$ be a morphism of $k_0$-schemes that is smooth of\nrelative dimension one, separated and quasi-compact, with affine\nfibres; thus every nonempty geometric fiber is a smooth affine curve.\nLet $\\mathcal F$ be a lisse Weil sheaf on $U_0$, punctually\n$\\iota$-pure of weight $w$, and let $i\\ge0$. Then every Frobenius\neigenvalue $\\alpha$ on the stalk of $R^ih_!\\mathcal F$ at a closed point\ny$ of degree $m$ satisfies $|\\iota(\\alpha)|\\le(q^m)^{(w+i)/2}$, i.e.\nthe punctual weight of $R^ih_!\\mathcal F$ at $y$ is at most $w+i$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-p-dl-general-relative-line/lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual.md",
  "place": "node lem-zl-relative-curve-punctual, order 2839"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-pbc-qbar-category",
  "def-weil-punctual-weights"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Fix a closed point $y\\in |Y_0|$ of degree $m$ and a geometric point $\\bar y$ above it. The compact-support base-change isomorphism [thm-cbc-qbar] for the Cartesian square formed by $U_{0,y}\\to U_0$ and $y\\to Y_0$ identifies the stalk of $R^ih_!\\mathcal F$ at $\\bar y$ with $H_c^i(U_{\\bar y},\\mathcal F|_{U_{\\bar y}})$. By [lem-tw-punctual-rescaling], the restriction is punctually pure of weight $w$ relative to $\\kappa(y)$, whose cardinality is $q^m$. Choose a finite extension $\\mathbf F_{q^{me}}/\\mathbf F_{q^m}$ over which the finitely many geometric connected components of the affine curve $U_{\\bar y}$ are defined. Each component is a smooth geometrically connected affine curve. Applying [thm-a1-curve-upper] to every component gives the bound $w+i$ for the eigenvalues of the $e$-th power of geometric Frobenius on the direct sum of their compactly supported cohomology groups. The direct sum has the same bound because its Frobenius action is block diagonal. Finally [lem-a1-weight-bound-constant-extension] descends this bound from $\\mathbf F_{q^{me}}$ to $\\mathbf F_{q^m}$, yielding $|\\iota(\\alpha)|\\le(q^m)^{(w+i)/2}$ and the equivalent punctual-weight assertion.",
   "uses": [
    "thm-cbc-qbar",
    "lem-tw-punctual-rescaling",
    "thm-a1-curve-upper",
    "lem-a1-weight-bound-constant-extension"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
